    "title": "Fort Valley State mourns a freshman scholar from Columbus - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Destiney Alston Fort Valley State University ,\n5 hours ago\nFORT VALLEY, Ga. ( WRBL ) — Fort Valley State University announced on Wednesday the death of a student from Columbus, Ga.\nFVSU officials stated that freshman Jame’la Moore passed away on Oct. 17.\nThe university released a statement on Facebook:\n“‘The FVSU community mourns the loss of our scholar, Jame’la Moore,” said FVSU President Paul Jones. “Our thoughts and prayers are with her family and all who knew and loved her.’”\nFVSU will be providing additional support or counseling for any students in need. Students are encouraged to visit the Wellness Center or call 833-646-1526.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WRBL.\n8",
